      "problem": "A player's height in a particular professional basketball league is normally distributed with a mean of $77$ inches and a standard deviation of $3.57$ inches.\nWhat is the probability that the height of a randomly selected player is more than $76$ inches but less than $78$ inches?\n\n*Hint: A table of values of $Φ(z)$ for different values of $z$ is given below, where $Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"5\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr> \n  <th width=\"25%\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$z$</th>\n  <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.06\\,$</th>\n  <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.07\\,$</th>\n  <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.08\\,$</th>\n</tr>\n<tr> \n  <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.1\\,$</th>\n  <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.5636\\,$ </td>\n  <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.5675\\,$ </td>\n  <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.5714\\,$ </td>\n</tr>\n<tr> \n  <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.2\\,$</th>\n    <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.6026\\,$ </td>\n    <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.6064\\,$ </td>\n    <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.6103\\,$ </td>\n</tr>\n<tr> \n  <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.3\\,$</th>\n  <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.6406\\,$ </td>\n  <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.6443\\,$ </td>\n  <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.6480\\,$ </td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</th>\n\n<th width=\"5%\"></th>\n\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"5\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr> \n  <th width=\"25%\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$z$</th>\n  <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.06\\,$</th>\n  <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.07\\,$</th>\n  <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.08\\,$</th>\n</tr>\n<tr> \n  <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,-0.3\\,$</th>\n  <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.3594\\,$ </td>\n  <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.3557\\,$ </td>\n  <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.3520\\,$ </td>\n</tr>\n<tr> \n  <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,-0.2\\,$</th>\n    <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.3974\\,$ </td>\n    <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.3936\\,$ </td>\n    <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.3897\\,$ </td>\n</tr>\n<tr> \n  <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,-0.1\\,$</th>\n  <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.4364\\,$ </td>\n  <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.4325\\,$ </td>\n  <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.4286\\,$ </td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</th>\n\n</tr>\n\n</tbody></table>",
      "worked_solution": "Let $X$ represent the height (in inches) of a randomly selected player. Then we have $X∼N(77,{3.57}^{2}).$\n\nWe want to find $P(76<X<78).$ First, we convert $X$ to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(76<X<78) & =P(\\frac{76-77}{3.57}<Z<\\frac{78-77}{3.57}) \\\\  & =P(-0.28<Z<0.28)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we express the required probability in terms of $Φ(z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-0.28<Z<0.28) & =P(Z<0.28)-P(Z\\le -0.28) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le 0.28)-P(Z\\le -0.28) \\\\  & =Φ(0.28)-Φ(-0.28)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the $z$-table, we see that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(0.28) & =0.6103 \\\\ Φ(-0.28) & =0.3897.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-0.28<Z<0.28) & =Φ(0.28)-Φ(-0.28) \\\\  & =0.6103-0.3897 \\\\  & =0.2206 \\\\  & ≈0.22\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the probability that the height of a randomly selected player is more than $76$ inches but less than $78$ inches is approximately $0.22.$",
